```
- Note `document.addEventListener('keydown'...)` for Esc; the existing one. Fine.
- The `composerContext` remove handler uses `closest`; the buttons are inside; good.
- The context buttons: `<button class="ctx-remove" data-remove=...>`; event listener. 
- The `data-remove` values.
- The `renderComposerContext` uses `escapeHtml`.
- The `cmCount` count.
- The + menu button active states.
- The `knowledge` button.
- The `model` buttons; `data-model`/`data-effort`.
- The model button label; `modelLabel.textContent`; `effortLabel`.
- The `model-btn` `aria-expanded`.
- The `composerPlus` `aria-expanded`.
- The `openComposerMenu` closes model; the `openModelMenu` closes composer.
- The outside click: `event.target.closest` works for elements; if target is SVG? `closest` exists on Element; event.target could be text? In click events, target is Element; fine.
- The document keydown Esc closes both; also the existing drawer; fine.
- The `fileInput` change; add names; close; showToast.
- The `cmAttach` click triggers file input; close menu; show? no.
- The attachments count; the file names duplicate; okay.
- The workflow buttons: if disabled, return. The `data-workflow` includes kb disabled; the listener still; check `btn.disabled`.
- The skills buttons: toggle; stays open.
- The knowledge: toggle.
- The + menu's `cm-manage` link: the document click might close; navigation.
- The model options:
  - `setModel`: update `chatModel`; modelLabel; all `[data-model]` active/aria; close; toast.
  - `setEffort`: update; effortLabel; all `[data-effort]`; close; toast.
- The initial model label/eefort from HTML. Good.
- The hash:
  ```js
  function applyWorkflowHash() {
    var match = window.location.hash.match(/workflow=([^&]+)/);
    if (!match) return;
    var id = decodeURIComponent(match[1]);
    var wf = CHAT_WORKFLOWS[id];
    if (!wf || wf.disabled) return;
    selectedWorkflow = id;
    renderComposerContext();
    showToast('已载入工作流：' + wf.name);
  }
  window.addEventListener('hashchange', applyWorkflowHash);
  ```
